    "body": "Audit of 22 Aug 2026.\n\n`stg_ads_sp_keyword_daily` and `stg_sales_traffic_asin_daily` were added in `58a5558` to repair a DAG that could not compile — three marts referenced them and neither existed. They were written under time pressure and, unlike the four earlier staging models, they have **no entry in `packages/dbt/models/staging/schema.yml`**, so `dbt build` runs zero tests against them.\n\nThat is exactly backwards: the two least reviewed models in the project are the two with no tests.\n\n### Tests to add\n\nFor both models:\n\n- `unique` on the surrogate grain, and `not_null` on `tenant_id` + `report_date`\n- a singular test asserting the dedupe worked: zero rows when grouping by the natural key with `having count(*) > 1`. Both models dedupe with `row_number() over (partition by ... order by loaded_at desc)`, and a wrong partition list is silent — it does not error, it just double-counts spend\n\nModel-specific:\n\n- `stg_ads_sp_keyword_daily`: `bid` must be `null` when absent and **never** `0` (a `0` bid would make `cpc` comparisons and the `raise_bid_profitable` factor arithmetic wrong). Test `accepted_range` on `top_of_search_impression_share` between 0 and 1 — it is divided by 100 in the model, and a source change back to a fraction would silently produce 0.003% values.\n- `stg_sales_traffic_asin_daily`: same `accepted_range` 0–1 for `buy_box_pct` and `unit_session_pct`. `avg_price_gross` is computed as `ordered_product_sales / units_ordered` — test that it is `null` and not infinite/zero when `units_ordered = 0`.\n\n### Wider check while in here\n\n`mart_sku_economics` and the three PPC marts have a `schema.yml`, but no test asserts the KPI divide-by-zero rule that the whole project depends on: **every ratio must be `null`, never `0`, when its denominator is 0.** A `0` ACOS reads as \"perfectly efficient\" and would make a zero-sales keyword look like the best performer in the account. Add one singular test per mart for that.\n\n### Done when\n\n- [ ] Both new models have `schema.yml` entries with the tests above\n- [ ] One singular test per mart asserts no ratio column is ever `0` while its denominator is `0`\n- [ ] `dbt build` passes with zero warnings\n\n**Backlog ref:** #12, #13",
